    "accordion_zxDydH": {
      "type": "accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "accor_item_qc6HAK": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can I wear the insoles with socks?",
            "content": "<p>The insoles are primarily designed to be worn on a bare foot. <strong>You can easily adjust the intensity with a sock <\/strong>— a thin sock softens the stimulation slightly, a thicker sock softens it more.<\/p><p>The sensation should be clear, but pleasant. Not painful.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_pNtHeV": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Who should not use active insoles? When to be careful?",
            "content": "<p>In most cases you can use active insoles without worry. If you have health issues, <strong>we recommend talking to a physiotherapist or doctor before using them<\/strong>. Especially if:<\/p><ul><li>you have significant or long-term foot pain<\/li><li>you’re recovering from an injury or surgery<\/li><li>you have neurological issues or loss of feeling in the feet<\/li><li>other more serious health conditions<\/li><\/ul>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_4FWKn3": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Are active insoles a medical device?",
            "content": "<p>No. Active insoles are not a medical device and are not a substitute for professional diagnosis, physiotherapy, or medical care. They are designed to support awareness of the feet and more active engagement when walking and standing.<\/p><p><strong>Before use, we recommend consulting a doctor or physiotherapist especially if you have:<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>diabetes, especially reduced feeling in the feet or neuropathy,<\/li><li>sensory disorders,<\/li><li>open wounds, sores, or skin problems,<\/li><li>an acute injury or pain,<\/li><li>significant neurological issues,<\/li><li>serious balance or coordination disorders,<\/li><li>uncertainty about whether the insoles are right for you.<\/li><\/ul><p>If you feel pain, worsening symptoms, or an unpleasant reaction, stop using them and talk to a specialist.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_UWBXGQ": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Which shoes are active insoles suitable for?",
            "content": "<p>They work best in barefoot and anatomically shaped shoes, where the feet have enough space for natural movement. You can also use them in ordinary shoes, as long as they are not too narrow or tight.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_ACkHqK": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can I trim the insoles to the shape of my shoe?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. You can easily adjust the insoles to the shape of your shoes. We recommend trimming them gradually, a little at a time. After trimming they can no longer be returned as unused goods, but the warranty still applies.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_REYhiD": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "When will I notice the first difference?",
            "content": "<p>Everyone is a little different. Some people notice a change the first time they put them on; for others it takes a while for the feet to get used to the new stimulus. That’s why we recommend starting slowly and gradually extending wearing time.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_ewTAwy": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Pomohou mi od bolesti nohou, kolen nebo zad?",
            "content": "<p>We unfortunately can’t promise that. But the feet affect movement of the whole body, so better engagement can contribute to more comfortable movement. If you have pain or other health issues, we recommend talking to a physiotherapist or doctor.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_DUwxtx": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can children use active insoles?",
            "content": "<p>Active insoles are currently designed for adults in sizes 37–46. We are not preparing a kids’ version at this time.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_WKKT47": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How should I care for shoe insoles?",
            "content": "<p>Air them out regularly and wipe with a damp cloth as needed. We don’t recommend machine washing or drying them on a direct heat source.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_8x8X6F": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What about returns and warranty claims?",
            "content": "<p>Active insoles are covered by the standard statutory warranty. Unused and undamaged insoles can be returned within 14 days. Note: if you trim them or otherwise modify them, they can no longer be returned as unused goods.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_eejHJ7": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can I use acupressure shoe insoles for exercise and running?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. You can use active insoles for strength training, running, and other movement. Gentle stimulation of the feet helps you better sense support and engage the whole body during exercise. When running, it can support a more active push-off and better ground feel. We recommend starting gradually and giving the feet time to adapt.<\/p>"
          }
        },
        "accor_item_ceYh8H": {
          "type": "accor_item",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Looking for a custom solution and made-to-measure insoles?",
            "content": "<p><strong>Every foot is unique<\/strong>. We designed active insoles to be as universal as possible. Still, they may not fit everyone perfectly. Some people may feel the stimulation more intensely, others more gently. For some, the arch support may be ideal; others will need a tailored solution.<\/p><p>If you want insoles adapted exactly to your feet, we also offer<a href=\"http:\/\/www.lukasklimpera.cz\/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"http:\/\/www.lukasklimpera.cz\/\"> a custom solution in cooperation with a physiotherapist<\/a>.<\/p>"
          }
        }
      },
